  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a tester, I want a tap on « Version » in Réglages (and in À propos) to copy the app's build details to the clipboard, so that I can paste them in a bug report and we know exactly which build, OS and device it is.\n\n### Today\n\n- `SettingsView.swift:172` and `AboutView.swift:24` show `LabeledContent(\"Version\", value: AppVersion.current.display)`; the values come from `CFBundleShortVersionString` and `CFBundleVersion` (`AboutModel.swift:9-12`). A tap does nothing.\n- No build records which commit it came from: the operator could not tell whether their Xcode build included cd049542 (2026-11-16).\n\n### Wanted (operator, 2026-11-16)\n\nA tap on the Version row copies one line or a short block, with no account, pseudo or other personal data:\n- app version and build (`CFBundleShortVersionString` (`CFBundleVersion`));\n- **the git commit** the app was built from: a short sha, plus `-dirty` if the tree had local changes. Inject it at build time (a build-phase script writing an Info.plist key, e.g. `HFRGitCommit`), and show `?` when it is absent (CI unsigned builds, a tarball);\n- the OS (`UIDevice.systemName` + `systemVersion`);\n- the device model code (`utsname.machine`, e.g. `iPhone18,2`; the simulator's `SIMULATOR_MODEL_IDENTIFIER`).\n\nThen a short confirmation (« Copié », and a VoiceOver announcement). The row also shows the commit, e.g. « 1.0 (42) · cd04954 ».\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A tap copies the text, in a stable format: `SwiftHFR <version> (<build>) · <commit> · <OS> · <model>`.\n- [ ] A test of the formatter covers a missing key, a missing commit and a simulator model.\n- [ ] The build script works for a local Xcode build and an unsigned CI build, never fails the build, and reads only `git rev-parse` (nothing secret). No new dependency.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
